# Repository-wide ignores.
#
# app/.gitignore covers the app tier from inside app/, but its `admin_console/.env`
# line predates the rename to `admin/` — and being scoped to app/, it could never
# have matched a sibling directory anyway. This file is what covers the admin
# tier, which is the tier whose .env currently carries the live Fernet key.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Runtime state. data/ holds secret.key, internal.key and flask_key.key in every
# tier; those three decrypt every bot token and every encrypted settings value in
# the shared database. No leading slash, so this matches at any depth — app/data/,
# admin/data/, and any copy an operator parks somewhere else.
data/

# Real .env files carry ENCRYPTION_KEY, the ATP password and INTERNAL_TOKEN. Only
# the committed templates are safe, so the negation has to come after the pattern
# that would otherwise swallow it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Backups rotate_key.py writes next to each .env before rewriting it. Each one
# holds the *previous* key, which still decrypts every value not yet re-encrypted
# — the same liability as the key itself, just with a timestamp on it.
*.bak-*

# Oracle wallet and any loose key material: credentials, same rule as data/.
Wallet_ATP/
wallet/
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key

# Operator backups taken before large changes contain copies of data/.
full backup done/

# Local-only editor and agent scratch state.
.claude/
